64 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 39 0 R
/T (The Bug Bounty Hunting Course is designed to equip learners with the skills required to identify, exploit, and report security vulnerabilities in web applications. As organizations increasingly rely on digital infrastructure, ethical hackers play a crucial role in helping companies secure their systems by identifying security flaws before malicious hackers can exploit them. This course provides a structured learning path for individuals looking to enter the bug bounty and ethical hacking industry, offering practical insights into hacking methodologies, vulnerability identification, and responsible disclosure practices.)
/E (The Bug Bounty Hunting Course is designed to equip learners with the skills required to identify, exploit, and report security vulnerabilities in web applications. As organizations increasingly rely on digital infrastructure, ethical hackers play a crucial role in helping companies secure their systems by identifying security flaws before malicious hackers can exploit them. This course provides a structured learning path for individuals looking to enter the bug bounty and ethical hacking industry, offering practical insights into hacking methodologies, vulnerability identification, and responsible disclosure practices.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
65 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 39 0 R
/T (Through a combination of theoretical knowledge and hands-on labs, participants will gain expertise in web application security testing, network security, and API exploitation. The course also introduces popular bug bounty platforms like HackerOne, Bugcrowd, and Open Bug Bounty, helping learners understand how to legally and ethically earn rewards by finding security vulnerabilities. By the end of this course, participants will have the skills to analyze, exploit, and report vulnerabilities effectively, making them valuable assets in the cybersecurity industry.)
/E (Through a combination of theoretical knowledge and hands-on labs, participants will gain expertise in web application security testing, network security, and API exploitation. The course also introduces popular bug bounty platforms like HackerOne, Bugcrowd, and Open Bug Bounty, helping learners understand how to legally and ethically earn rewards by finding security vulnerabilities. By the end of this course, participants will have the skills to analyze, exploit, and report vulnerabilities effectively, making them valuable assets in the cybersecurity industry.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
